# Every table the `pm` schema actually has, read from the catalogue. One row per table.
#
# The population of the domain-object contract
#   The database is the only honest source for it. diagrams/domain_objects.sqlc declares what each
#   relational object renders as; this is what there is to declare about. Parsing `CREATE TABLE`
#   out of the `.ddl` would be a second reading of the same file the schema was loaded from, so a
#   table added and never loaded would still appear and the contract would agree with a database
#   that does not exist.
#
# The one relation here that reads outside `pm`
#   That is the reason for it: a contract needs a population it did not write.
#   `information_schema` is SQL-standard and every engine has it.
-- information_schema.tables restricted to the schema this model owns.
SELECT t.table_name::text AS object
FROM information_schema.tables t
WHERE t.table_schema = 'pm' AND t.table_type = 'BASE TABLE'
